From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:37:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] airconv, d3d12: 64-bit atomic min/max without Metal's native
 one; heap resources

Metal's 64-bit atomic min/max needs Apple8 (M2) or later. D3D12 pipelines now
pass SM50_SHADER_FLAG_NO_NATIVE_ATOMIC64_MINMAX on older GPUs, and the converter
then takes the lock word for them like for the other 64-bit atomics. Any shader
with 64-bit buffer atomics gets the lock table bound; whether it's used is
decided at compile time.

OPTIONS11 reports AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported: heap buffers
reach the same lock table. airconv -no-native-atomic64-minmax compiles as for
such a GPU.
---
